 a lads gun interacted  with a field generator shield produced  by the Holtzman effect sub atomic fusion  occurred the results were catastrophic  because the use of shields was so  widespread throughout the empire other  types of weapons were typically used  over last guns in order to avoid these  kinds of nuclear reactions before the  time of the god emperor when the  padishah Emperor still reigned most  soldiers preferred the use of swords and  knives in combat when utilized correctly  such weapons could safely penetrate body  shields Duncan Idaho who attended the  genus school trained Paul Atreides in  swordsmanship the swords masters of the  genus school were considered the  greatest warriors in the universe the  best of the impure sardick our soldiers  could match up to a level tin genus  swordsman the craft of swordsmanship was  respected in the Imperium and many of  the Great Houses of the far for Lucius  employed a swords Master of the genus  school on the planet Arrakis however  especially in the desert devices such as  louse guns and mala pistols were more  common since the use of shields was  impossible in the deep desert due to the  maddening effect that the Holtzman  effect had on the great worms of dune  the freeman who lived their lives  roaming the deep desert often made use  of mala pistols which could fire darts a  considerable distance the Fremen also  made use of blades called Kriss knives a  Kriss knife was a blade carved from the  tooth of a dead sand worm these weapons  were sacred to the Freeman once the  blade was drawn blood must be shed  it was also forbidden for an outsider to  lay eyes upon an unsheathed blade the  Freeman would also often poison the tips  of the blades hunter seekers were an  extremely dangerous and very common  assassination weapon used among the  noble houses of the Imperium the  children of nobility learned about such  devices at very young ages the device  would be operated from another location  and depend upon motion detection to see  its target once a target was detected  the device would burrow directly into  the targets closest vital organ killing  them instantly  immediately after the but Larian jihad  when all thinking machines have been  destroyed the rulers of the Imperium  converged to form the great convention a  treaty which reserved the use of Atomics  for a nonhuman entity the agreement said  that due to the catastrophic history  that nuclear weapons had among human  society humans would never use such  weapons on each other but instead on  non-human threats should they ever  appear only the Great Houses would be  allowed to possess Atomics henceforth  the great convention stated use of  Atomics against humans shall be cause  for planetary obliteration in the book  dune Paul Atreides finds somewhat of a  loophole he uses Atomics not on humans  but to blast a whole  the shield wall of Arrakeen after Paul  became Emperor the Imperium adherence to  the great convention had lessened  considerably Atomics had not been the  only weapons prohibited by the great  convention but all weapons of mass  destruction including stone burners  stone burners were terrible weapons  which not only caused great destruction  but released a type of ray that  destroyed the eye tissue of anything  within several miles a stone burner  detonated at the core of a planet would  cause a reaction leading to the total  destruction of the world the weapon  worked by harnessing atomic energy it  would create fusion setting off an  atomic source and absorbing the sources  energy it would create a disastrous  result the assassins Handbook and in a  universe work supposedly contained a  compilation of commonly used poisons  permitted during the war of assassins  and the weapons which were permitted as  well the war of assassins referred to  the form of warfare that was allowed  under the great convention the spacing  guild also helped maintain peace the  guilds monopoly on space travel meant  that they could deny access to those  that were disruptive 5,000 years into  the saga by the time of the honoured  matras the guilds monopoly on space  travel had been broken and the great  convention was no longer honored the  matras utilize a weapon possessing  tremendous power when activated it  created a blast of incredible heat  capable of scorching the surface of  entire worlds the honored mot Ray's  brought the weapon out of the scattering  and intended to use it to subdue the  Binnie Jesuit sisterhood many science  fiction writers tend to agree that war  is a part of human nature even thousands  of years in the future humankind still  must contend with its self-destructive  disposition the timeline of the dune  saga indicates that humankind has some  difficulty evolving past these patterns  and even though peace can be maintained  for some time society tends to trend  towards violence the honored MOT Ray's  represent a version of the many Jesuit  who had lost their way surrendering to  their most volatile instincts and  undoubtedly setting themselves on a  clear path  for annihilation thank you guys so much  for watching make sure you like and  subscribe if you enjoyed the content and  if you want to support this channel  click the patreon link in the  description

